note fuelc: charge n to the function's fuel at the construct on line ln, before anything of it expands; a
note total above 65536 is error 14 on line ln (E14, E16)
fn fuelc ln ulong n ulong to void
if gt add get fuel 0 n 65536
put line 0 ln
note d2site 309|fuelc: capacity exceeded (the host refused to grow the compiler's arena or its memory ceiling OMC_MEMORY_MAX was reached, value nesting past omc's own stack, the program image, or an OM-2 expansion bound); condition if gt add get fuel 0 n 65536
put d2site 0 309
fail 14
end
put fuel 0 add get fuel 0 n
end

note s_unr: the end of an unrolled body: read it again with the next value of i, or close the block
fn s_unr i ulong to void
eol
it = add get a_ar add get a_rb 64 i 1
if lt it get a_ar add get a_rb 65 i
fuelc sub a_g 63 i 1 1
put a_ar add get a_rb 64 i it
